window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["00"]={"https://theconversation.com/pasifika-women-are-making-rugby-league-history-but-what-about-the-next-generation-295741":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:38Z","sha":"cfa2cf6e87d57aee27e082d1728625785b679a64e307a5f7cb33afdff2572f1a","read":"https://theconversation.com/pasifika-women-are-making-rugby-league-history-but-what-about-the-next-generation-295741","bytes":182964,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Pasifika women are making rugby league history. But what about the next generation?","by":[{"n":"Sierra Keung","r":"Lecturer in Sport and Recreation, Auckland University of Technology"},{"n":"Mihi Joy Nemani","r":"Senior Lecturer, Te Huataki Waiora School of Health, University of Waikato"}],"pub":"2026-11-12T18:21:47Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["For ",["Fetu Samoa","https://samoaglobalnews.com/1history-made-fetu-samoa-qualify-for-rugby-league-world-cup-semi-finals-for-first-time/"]," and ",["Fiji Bulikula","https://fijisun.com.fj/sports/rugby/bulikula-eye-jillaroos-upset-after-making-history-at-rlwc"],", the ",["2026 Women’s Rugby League World Cup","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2026_Women%27s_Rugby_League_World_Cup"]," marked a historic breakthrough, with both nations reaching the semifinals for the first time."]},{"k":"p","s":["While each team came up short against ",["New Zealand’s Kiwi Ferns","https://www.nzherald.co.nz/sport/rugby-league/kiwi-ferns-v-fetu-samoa-live-updates-womens-rugby-league-world-cup-semi-final/CQMWMYQFNVBYDKXAZKPJL3E6PY/"]," and ",["Australia’s Jillaroos","https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/nov/08/australia-jillaroos-fiji-womens-rugby-league-world-cup-semi-final-match-report"]," respectively last weekend, their strong showing throughout the tournament highlighted ",["the depth of Pasifika talent in the code","https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/pacific/1793479/pacific-women-s-squads-packed-with-nrl-experience-for-rugby-league-world-cup"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Interestingly, players of Pacific heritage featured across all four semifinal teams, reflecting the pathways that have enabled Pasifika women to compete at the highest level."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many players representing Pacific nations have advanced through development systems in Australia and New Zealand. However, opportunities within Pacific countries themselves remain much more limited."]},{"k":"p","s":["So what pathways are needed to ensure the next generation of Pasifika players can thrive closer to home?"]},{"k":"h","s":["Paths to the top"]},{"k":"p","s":["Building better pathways means more than identifying top talent. Girls need opportunities to enter the game and keep playing. This starts with local clubs, coaching, facilities and regular competitions providing a foundation for those hoping to reach elite levels."]},{"k":"p","s":["Currently, the routes players take to international rugby league vary considerably. Fiji’s world cup squad has just one locally based player, while Samoa’s team draws heavily on talent developed through ",["Australia’s National Rugby League Women’s Premiership","https://www.nrl.com/nrlw/"]," (NRLW) system."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meanwhile, Papua New Guinea’s Orchids include both Australian-based players and those who have advanced through domestic clubs and competitions."]},{"k":"p","s":["But where players are based only tells part of the story. It reveals little about where they first played, who supported their development, or the connections they maintain with Pasifika communities."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Research with Pasifika men","https://www.jstor.org/stable/24809728"]," in Australian rugby league highlights the importance of migration, family, faith, culture and national allegiance in their experiences of the sport. While women’s experiences differ, the findings suggest pathways into international rugby league are rarely straightforward, or confined to a single country."]},{"k":"h","s":["Keeping women in the game"]},{"k":"p","s":["The need to boost opportunities within Pacific nations comes ",["as the Australian government commits","https://www.pm.gov.au/media/scoring-tries-and-strengthening-ties-pacific"]," A$250 million over ten years to the Pacific Rugby League Partnership with Papua New Guinea, Samoa, Tonga and Fiji. Plans include girls’ and national competitions, development pathways and academies, alongside education, leadership and employment opportunities."]},{"k":"p","s":["But how much of that investment will reach women and girls? And will Pasifika women have a meaningful say in how these programmes are designed and delivered? Much will depend on how the funding is allocated and what support is available on the ground."]},{"k":"p","s":["Research offers some insights into what makes sporting opportunities accessible."]},{"k":"p","s":["A ",["netball-for-development programme","https://www.academia.edu/95772657/Schulenkorf_N_Sherry_E_Siefken_K_Tauhalaliku_U_and_Richards_J_2022_Health_Interventions_as_Vehicles_for_Increased_Sport_Participation_for_Girls_and_Women_Socio_Managerial_Insights_from_a_Netball_for_Development_Program_in_Tonga_Journal_of_Sport_for_Development_10_1_25_39"]," in Tonga highlights the importance of family and community support, access to facilities and equipment, regular competitions and the volunteers who keep local sport running."]},{"k":"p","s":["More ",["recent research in Fiji","https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/sports-and-active-living/articles/10.3389/fspor.2026.1855393/full"]," found that while sport can open doors for young people, young women face particular barriers, including domestic responsibilities, financial pressures and gender expectations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Practical support for women’s health is also important. A ",["study","https://journals.sagepub.com/doi/10.1177/10126902251351181"]," involving Pacific sportswomen found that cultural expectations and family attitudes influence how menstruation is understood and discussed, as well as the information and support available to women in sporting environments."]},{"k":"p","s":["These findings highlight the need for investment beyond elite competitions and academies. Without accessible facilities, regular opportunities to play and support that responds to women’s circumstances, even well-funded development programmes risk leaving many girls behind."]},{"k":"h","s":["Making the next play"]},{"k":"p","s":["The knowledge, relationships and experience women gain through playing can open doors to coaching, officiating, administration and leadership."]},{"k":"p","s":["Jillaroos head coach ",["Jess Skinner","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-10-11/jillaroos-coach-jessica-skinner-2026-rugby-league-world-cup/107098594"]," has followed such a path. A Barkindji and Māori woman, she progressed from grassroots women’s rugby league in regional New South Wales to leading Australia’s national team. Along the way, she relied on family sacrifices, community support and mentors who helped her advance. She is also the only female head coach at this world cup."]},{"k":"p","s":["For Pasifika women, opportunities to lead ",["are closely connected","https://indd.adobe.com/view/786559fb-d4b9-4548-a183-45e4ac830ef8"]," to culture, family, faith and community."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet mainstream leadership models do not always recognise Pacific approaches, potentially overlooking women with valuable knowledge and experience. More culturally grounded development programmes would help bring these women into coaching, administration and decision-making roles."]},{"k":"p","s":["Women should not have to choose between pursuing professional opportunities overseas and contributing to the game at home. They should be able to do both. This builds stronger connections between domestic and international competitions allowing skills, experience and expertise to benefit rugby league across the Pacific."]},{"k":"p","s":["Success, then, shouldn’t be measured solely by the number of Pasifika women reaching the NRLW or international competition. It should also be evident in stronger local competitions, more women in coaching and leadership roles, and greater opportunities for the next generation to enter and remain in the game."]},{"k":"p","s":["Samoa and Fiji’s historic World Cup campaigns have shown what Pasifika women can achieve. The task now is to ensure that success translates into lasting opportunities for those who follow."]}],"chars":5503},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/croatia":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"ebf23e290ad96709f34521867e7f16c936597561e498e1fa42231f80c1ee37bf","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/croatia","bytes":72125,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Croatia travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-05T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-11T10:18:43+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/croatia/email-signup"]," for Croatia when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Croatia set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Croatian Embassy in the UK","https://mvep.gov.hr/uk"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Croatia follows ",["Schengen area rules","https://europa.eu/youreurope/citizens/travel/entry-exit/non-eu-nationals/index_en.htm"],". Your passport must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have a ‘date of issue’ less than 10 years before the date you arrive – if you renewed your passport before 1 October 2018, it might have a date of issue that is more than 10 years ago, making it invalid for entry to the Schengen area"]},{"k":"li","s":["have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the day you plan to leave the Schengen area (the expiry date does not need to be within 10 years of the date of issue)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["travel without a visa to the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/travel-to-eu-schengen-area"],", which includes Croatia, for up to 90 days in any 180-day period. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"li","s":["for short-term studies or training"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["requirements for working in Croatia","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/travel-to-croatia-for-work"]," are different."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling to other Schengen countries make sure your whole visit is within the 90-day visa-free limit. Visits to Schengen countries in the 180 days before you travel count towards your 90 days. If you overstay the 90-day visa-free limit, you may be banned from entering Schengen countries for up to 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["At Croatian border control, you may also need to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["show proof of your accommodation, for example, a hotel booking confirmation or proof of address for a second home"]},{"k":"li","s":["show proof of your travel insurance"]},{"k":"li","s":["show a return or onward ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["prove that you have enough money for your stay – the amount varies depending on your accommodation"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Staying longer than 90 days in a 180-day period"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer, you must meet the Croatian government’s entry requirements. Check which type of visa or work permit you need with the ",["Croatian Embassy in the UK","https://mvep.gov.hr/consular-information-107317/general-visa-information-107319/107319"],". See the Croatian Ministry of the Interior’s guidance on ",["work permits","https://mup.gov.hr/radne-dozvole/286764"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in Croatia with a residence permit or long-stay visa, this does not count towards your 90-day visa-free limit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about ",["entry processes if you live in Croatia","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-croatia#passports-and-travel"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["New Schengen entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area."]},{"k":"p","s":["This means that when you travel into the Schengen area for short stays, you may need to register your biometric details, such as fingerprints and a photo. There is no cost for EES registration."]},{"k":"p","s":["On your first visit into a Schengen country, you may be asked to register your details at a special booth before proceeding to the immigration desk. Follow directions from your travel operator or the staff at your port of entry. You may also need to provide either your fingerprint or photo when you leave the Schengen area. Children aged 11 or younger will not have their fingerprints scanned but can be required to have their photo taken."]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need to take any action before you arrive at the border on entry to the Schengen area, but EES may take each passenger extra time to complete so be prepared to wait longer than usual at the border and to allow more time for immigration controls when you depart the Schengen area. If you are departing the Schengen area by plane, allow extra time to reach your departure gate as EES checks may take place before boarding."]},{"k":"p","s":["EES is replacing the previous system of manually stamping passports when visitors arrive in the Schengen area for short stays. You may be asked to input biometric details every time you enter or exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter the Schengen area through the Port of Dover, Eurotunnel at Folkestone or Eurostar at St Pancras International, any information will be taken at the border before you leave the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your digital EES record is valid for 3 years."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["information on the EU Entry/Exit System and to understand which countries are in the Schengen area","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/eu-entryexit-system"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are long-term resident in a Schengen country, you are exempt from EES in all Schengen countries. The full list of EES exemptions is on ",["the EU’s official Travel Europe website.","https://travel-europe.europa.eu/en/ees/to-whom-does-ees-not-apply"]]},{"k":"p","s":["If you believe you have been incorrectly entered into EES or your record of time spent in the Schengen area is incorrect, approach border officials when you next cross the Schengen border and request a correction. If you are exempt, carry documentation confirming your status. If you believe your time spent in the Schengen area has been recorded incorrectly, raise this with border officials and be prepared to provide supporting evidence if requested."]},{"k":"h","s":["Croatia-Slovenia border crossings"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are checks at Slovenia’s borders with Croatia. If you are travelling from Croatia to Slovenia, check ",["travel advice for Slovenia","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/slovenia/entry-requirements"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Croatia guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/59/croatia#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Registering with the police"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your accommodation provider must register your arrival in Croatia with the police within 48 hours. Your hotel will normally register you. If your accommodation provider is unable to do this for you, ",["fill in and print form obrazac 16a (PDF)","https://mup.gov.hr/UserDocsImages/dokumenti/stranci/2022/Obrazac-prijave-i-odjave-smjestaja-boravista-i-prebivalista-za-drz-trecih-zemalja-(Obrazac-16a).pdf"],". You must hand in the completed form at a police station. Alternatively, you should go to the nearest police station with the owner of the accommodation to register your address in Croatia."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods that can be brought into and taken out of Croatia","https://carina.gov.hr/featured/information-for-passengers-natural-persons/relief-from-duties-and-restrictions/6715"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food into Croatia"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take ",["meat, milk or products containing them into EU countries","https://ec.europa.eu/food/animals/animalproducts/personal_imports_en"],". There are some exceptions such as powdered baby milk, baby food and special foods or pet feed required for medical reasons."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Croatia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the ",["value is 10,000 euros or more","https://carina.gov.hr/featured/information-for-passengers-natural-persons/bringing-cash-and-goods-across-the-border/6711"],". You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you. If you do not, your money could be seized when you leave."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Croatia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Croatia, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreigners."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime levels are low and violent crime is rare."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourists have been overcharged at certain ‘gentlemen’s clubs’, sometimes by thousands of euros, and threatened with violence if they refuse to pay."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pickpockets operate in tourist areas. Avoid carrying large sums of cash, do not leave valuables unattended and use hotel safes if possible."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Attacks and sexual assaults in taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been reports of sexual assaults in taxis in Croatia. To reduce risk and help prevent potential assaults:"]},{"k":"li","s":["take a photo of the inside, where the number of the taxi is visible, and send it to a friend or someone else"]},{"k":"li","s":["share your ride status on the taxi app"]},{"k":"li","s":["make a call while in the taxi telling someone which taxi it is and where you are going"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Large gatherings, including football matches"]},{"k":"p","s":["Large gatherings and public events are overwhelmingly safe and peaceful in Croatia, including sporting events. However, there are periodic cases of violence between football fans around matches. Care should be taken near football stadiums around match times, especially “derby” matches, and you should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid large crowds"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local news reports"]},{"k":"li","s":["comply with instructions from police"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you feel uncomfortable, leave the area immediately."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry your passport or, if you’re a resident, your Croatian ID card. Keep a copy of your passport’s photo page in a safe place."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Antisocial behaviour"]},{"k":"p","s":["In some Croatian town centres, including tourist destinations like Split and Dubrovnik, you can get on-the-spot fines for behaviour seen as inappropriate, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["drinking alcohol or using drugs in public spaces"]},{"k":"li","s":["sleeping in public spaces"]},{"k":"li","s":["urinating or vomiting in public spaces"]},{"k":"li","s":["walking through towns shirtless or in swimwear"]},{"k":"li","s":["wearing clothing that promotes drug use"]},{"k":"li","s":["climbing on monuments"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also be fined up to 4,000 euros for public order disturbances, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["fighting"]},{"k":"li","s":["verbal abuse such as shouting or arguing"]},{"k":"li","s":["drunken behaviour"]},{"k":"li","s":["belittling or insulting police officers or other public officials"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties. Carrying cannabis for personal use has been decriminalised but if found on you or in your apartment, you will be asked to pay sometimes heavy fines."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Croatia have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Unexploded mines"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you travel outside the tourist resorts, beware of unexploded mines in previously war-affected areas, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Eastern Slavonia"]},{"k":"li","s":["Brod-Posavina County"]},{"k":"li","s":["Karlovac County"]},{"k":"li","s":["areas around Zadar County"]},{"k":"li","s":["more remote areas of the Plitvice Lakes National Park"]},{"k":"p","s":["For more information about mine-affected areas, visit the ",["Civil Protection website","https://civilna-zastita.gov.hr/UserDocsImages/145"]," (in Croatian) or contact the Civil Protection offices."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling in these areas, do not walk on uncultivated land or step off the marked paths. If in doubt, get local advice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiking and mountaineering"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re hiking in the mountains, get expert advice from local guides, however tame the mountain might seem. Weather in the Croatian mountains can change quickly, even in summer. Temperatures can get very low overnight."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of getting lost in the mountains when out hiking alone and using unmarked paths. Read the ",["Croatian Mountain Rescue tips on mountaineering","https://www.hgss.hr/en/"],", follow their X at ",["Hrvatska GSS","https://x.com/hrvatskaGSS"]," and see their maps. If you get into trouble, call the emergency number 112 for help from the Croatian Mountain Rescue Service."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Music festivals"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many music festivals are held in Croatia each year. Follow the advice of police and local authorities when attending events and take care of your valuables if attending a festival or large concert. Find out how to enjoy festivals safely with the ",["festival travel checklist","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/festival-travel-checklist"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to drive in Croatia, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in RAC’s Croatia guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/croatia/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["having your headlights on and dipped when driving a car from 1 November until 31 March, even during daytime"]},{"k":"li","s":["driving with dipped headlights year-round on scooters and motorcycles"]},{"k":"li","s":["using winter tyres between 15 November and 15 April"]},{"k":"li","s":["carrying a fluorescent vest in the car, not in the boot – you must wear the vest while attending to a breakdown"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Croatia for up to one year. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are visiting Croatia, you may be able to use your ",["Blue Badge","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/blue-badge-using-it-in-the-eu/using-a-blue-badge-in-the-european-union"]," in some circumstances. Check local parking rules."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Croatian Automobile Association lists ",["current traffic hazards","https://www.hak.hr/en#traffic-flow-and-road-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink-driving is a serious offence in Croatia. If you’re found with more than 0.05% of alcohol in your blood (in England it’s 0.08%) you will get a fine, and you may lose your licence and get a prison sentence. The alcohol limit is zero for drivers under the age of 24."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not drink alcohol if you’re in charge of a yacht or boat. There are heavy penalties for being caught drunk in charge of a boat and a zero-tolerance approach."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must sail by the most direct route to a port of entry when entering Croatian territorial waters."]},{"k":"p","s":["Authorities can arrest you for entering a non-designated entry port without telling them. If you cannot use the correct entry port, contact the local harbour master or the police before entering Croatia."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in Croatia, including on a boat, your presence in Croatia must be registered with the police. If you’re travelling with a tour operator, they should do this for you. Otherwise, you must ",["fill in and print form obrazac 16a (PDF)","https://mup.gov.hr/UserDocsImages/dokumenti/stranci/2022/Obrazac-prijave-i-odjave-smjestaja-boravista-i-prebivalista-za-drz-trecih-zemalja-(Obrazac-16a).pdf"]," and hand it in at a police station."]},{"k":"p","s":["All captains must have an ",["International Certificate of Competence","https://www.rya.org.uk/knowledge/abroad/icc"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],". Please follow advice from local authorities and monitor ",["Croatian Meteorological and Hydrological Service","https://meteo.hr/index_en.php"]," forecasts."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Wildfires are common during Croatia’s hot and dry summers. They can be highly dangerous and unpredictable. The situation can change quickly. Take care when visiting or driving through woodland and forest areas. If you see a fire, call the emergency services on 112."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be cautious if you are in or near an area affected by wildfires:"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the advice of local authorities and emergency services"]},{"k":"li","s":["call the Croatian emergency services on 112 if you are in immediate danger"]},{"k":"li","s":["for further information, see Croatia’s ",["Civil Protection website","https://civilna-zastita.gov.hr/en"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Intentionally causing a fire is illegal in Croatia and you could be fined 2,000 to 20,000 euros, or even given a prison sentence. You could also be fined for unintentionally causing a fire. To avoid starting wildfires:"]},{"k":"li","s":["leave no litter, especially not glass which is known to start fires"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not light barbecues. From 1 June to 31 October it is illegal to set outdoor fires and barbecues except in designated areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["properly extinguish cigarette ends and do not leave any rubbish behind, particularly empty bottles, as these are known to start fires"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes in Croatia can be strong and cause deaths and damage to infrastructure. In recent years, there have been earthquakes in Zagreb and in Petrinja, near Sisak in central Croatia. Both caused extensive damage to buildings and infrastructure and loss of life. Heavily damaged buildings, which are not always signposted, may be unstable."]},{"k":"p","s":["Small tremors also happen several times a month throughout the year. Most pass without consequence. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Floods"]},{"k":"p","s":["Flash floods can happen with very little warning and lead to dangerous water flows and disruption to transport and other networks. There is the highest risk of flooding in central Croatia, between Karlovac and Slavonski Brod. Monitor ",["Croatian Meteorological and Hydrological Service","https://meteo.hr/index_en.php"]," forecasts, as well as traffic conditions with the Croatian Automobile authority and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Croatia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/59/croatia#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Croatia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/59/croatia#General_Information"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["biting insects and ticks"]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Croatia"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical facilities in Croatia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/medical-facilities-in-croatia"],", where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["To get medically necessary state healthcare in Croatia, you need a Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC) or a European Health Insurance Card (EHIC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS’s ",["getting healthcare abroad webpage","https://www.nhs.uk/using-the-nhs/healthcare-abroad/apply-for-a-free-uk-global-health-insurance-card-ghic/"]," has details about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to apply for a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to get temporary cover if you lose your card or it does not arrive in time"]},{"k":"li","s":["who qualifies for a new EHIC instead of a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["what treatment counts as medically necessary"]},{"k":"p","s":["A GHIC or EHIC is not an alternative to travel insurance. In Croatia there is always a charge for treatment, which can be up to 530 euros. You may have other costs your GHIC or EHIC does not cover, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["changes to travel and accommodation bookings"]},{"k":"li","s":["additional standard costs for treatment"]},{"k":"li","s":["medical repatriation to the UK"]},{"k":"li","s":["treatment that is ruled non-urgent"]},{"k":"li","s":["private healthcare"]},{"k":"li","s":["private clinics"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Croatia","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/healthcare-in-croatia"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travel-and-mental-health"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Croatia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you’re involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Croatia"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Croatia"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Croatia"]," in Croatia"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with ",["a death in Croatia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/croatia-bereavement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Croatia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/croatia-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/croatia/british-embassy-zagreb"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/croatia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Croatia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-croatia"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":20381,"change":"Updated information on European Entry-Exit System (EES) (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/jd-vance-singled-out-iran-war-for-midterm-rout-he-didnt-say-what-should-happen-next-in-conflict-295938":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"293b6d6cf87508fbadbaeb857cb8bdb094c7828cbfd777bed21ad98abf239008","read":"https://theconversation.com/jd-vance-singled-out-iran-war-for-midterm-rout-he-didnt-say-what-should-happen-next-in-conflict-295938","bytes":188368,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"JD Vance singled out Iran War for midterm rout – he didn’t say what should happen next in conflict","by":[{"n":"Javed Ali","r":"Associate Professor of Practice of Public Policy, University of Michigan"}],"pub":"2026-11-06T00:31:57Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["While votes were still being counted ",["in the U.S. midterm elections","https://theconversation.com/epic-blue-wave-helps-democrats-take-congress-in-overwhelming-rebuke-to-president-trump-295830"],", administration figures in Washington were already inviting speculation over how the results might be ",["connected to the conflict with Iran","https://theconversation.com/with-control-of-congress-heres-how-democrats-could-stop-trumps-war-in-iran-295954"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["On the morning after the election, Vice President JD Vance ",["wrote on X","https://x.com/JDVance/status/2118004988433641835"]," that the major reason for the dramatic loss for Republicans was the American public’s opposition to the war. “Everyone knows why we lost. And any honest conversation about where we go from here must start there,” he wrote, in reference to the ongoing conflict that began with U.S.-Israeli airstrikes against Iran in late February 2026."]},{"k":"p","s":["While it is rare for a vice president to make such a critical proclamation about their own administration’s policy, President Donald Trump later stated that ",["he did not disagree with Vance’s appraisal","https://www.the-sun.com/news/17256408/jd-vance-blames-midterm-elections-loss-iran-war-trump/"]," of the role that frustration with the Iran war played in voters’ minds."]},{"k":"p","s":["But whether this changes Trump’s view on next steps in the ongoing conflict remains unclear. Reporting over the past few weeks has indicated that the U.S. military has been actively preparing options and ",["increasing capabilities in the Persian Gulf region","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/10/21/us/politics/us-israel-renewed-iran-strikes.html"]," in the event the president directs a resumption of hostilities."]},{"k":"p","s":["As an ",["expert on Middle East affairs","https://fordschool.umich.edu/faculty/javed-ali"]," and a former senior official at the National Security Council during the first Trump administration, I’m aware that months of conflict have failed to bring Iran to its knees, force regime change or militarily defeat a perceived threat to U.S. assets and allies. Escalating now is unlikely to change those realities – and it carries the additional risk of further damaging Republicans in the eyes of Americans voters as they turn toward the 2028 presidential race."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even if Trump were to ratchet up the conflict, moreover, it’s unclear how much wiggle room he’ll have come January facing a Democratic Congress almost ",["uniformly opposed to the war","https://www.cnn.com/2026/11/04/politics/video/jeffries-says-ending-iran-war-will-be-top-of-house-democrats-agenda"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Sunk costs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Part of the issue facing Iran war hawks in Washington now is that the conflict has caused serious setbacks for the regime in Tehran without satisfying the officially stated strategic reasons for going to war."]},{"k":"p","s":["They argue that pulling back now – as welcome as that might be for Americans struggling with the associated rising cost of fuel – may allow Iran to rebuild before the conflict is “won.” Moreover, it would render the military and reputational costs already sunk by Washington as wasted."]},{"k":"p","s":["Among the achievements of this war touted by the Trump administration has been the ",["death of former Supreme Leader Ali Khameini","https://www.cnn.com/2026/02/28/middleeast/ayatollah-khamenei-iran-killed-airstrike-intl-latam"],", along with the killing of scores of ",["senior leaders within the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps","https://www.timesofisrael.com/israel-says-irgc-navy-commander-killed-iranian-top-envoy-said-removed-from-hit-list/"]," – including individuals like the ",["former head of Iran’s National Security Council Ali Larijani","https://www.aljazeera.com/features/2026/3/3/who-is-ali-larijani-the-iranian-official-promising-a-lesson-to-the-us"],". Significant elements of Iran’s air defense and radar network, ",["ballistic missile and drone production, and storage and launch sites","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/16/us-says-it-has-destroyed-iran-missile-capacity-how-is-iran-still-shooting"]," have also been destroyed. And Iran’s ",["already outdated navy and air force","https://www.aerotime.aero/articles/iran-dwindling-air-force-can-jets-still-fly-drone-attacks"]," has been further degraded."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meanwhile, the U.S.-imposed ",["naval blockade","https://www.centcom.mil/MEDIA/PUBLIC-RELEASES/Article/4542098/us-forces-to-resume-naval-blockade-against-iran/"]," against Iranian-linked shipping in the Persian Gulf cut off a crucial lifeline for Iran’s economy. And ",["additional sanctions and economic penalties","https://www.state.gov/iran-sanctions/"]," imposed by Washington have served to ",["further devalue Iran’s currency","https://finance.yahoo.com/economy/articles/iran-currency-getting-obliterated-regime-214000456.html"]," and ",["deprive Iran of additional financial links","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/14/how-do-iranians-move-money-abroad-to-avoid-us-sanctions"]," to the international banking system."]},{"k":"h","s":["Down but not out"]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet for all the U.S. successes in degrading the Iranian military by limitless aerial bombardment and the significant financial pressure against the Iranian economy, an obvious endgame remains elusive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite weakening the Iranian government – now led by Ali Khameinei’s son, Mojtaba, and a ",["new echelon of senior IRGC commanders","https://www.cnn.com/2026/06/05/middleeast/iran-supreme-leader-adviser-mohsen-rezaei-interview-intl"]," – the Islamic Republic remains intact. Moreover, it ",["still possesses enough ballistic missiles and drones","https://www.jpost.com/middle-east/iran-news/article-911221"]," to hold the region at risk, while continuing ",["to impose significant control over its population","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/10/25/irans-authorities-take-self-sacrifice-mobilisation-campaign-nationwide"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meanwhile, U.S. military spending continues to rise. In September, the U.S. Congressional Budget Office assessed that the ",["military costs of the Iran War had already totaled US$38 billion","https://www.cbo.gov/publication/62756"],". Since then, that ",["number has only increased","https://www.militarytimes.com/news/2026/10/28/us-costs-of-iran-war-rise-to-over-47-billion-according-to-pentagon-estimate/"],". And that is to say nothing of the associated global economic costs that have resulted from Iran’s de facto closure of the Strait of Hormuz – a key shipping route for oil and gas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Should Trump decide to change course on Iran, he – and others – may think that the money, effort and ",["lives of 19 American servicemen","https://www.militarynews.com/news/national/families-of-some-us-troops-killed-in-the-iran-wars-deadliest-strike-absent-from-white/article_2ddea9b5-b98f-5f10-bd28-3a1b82aa2621.html"]," killed in the conflict would have been spent with no obvious objective achieved. Yet continued military expenditure with no strategic endgame could only magnify those same costs."]},{"k":"p","s":["To Iran, the midterm results have not changed its public position. Mojtaba Khameini has issued statements ",["directing the IRGC to widen the conflict in the region and perhaps beyond","https://www.newsweek.com/khamenei-orders-iran-military-response-without-geographical-limitations-12644735"]," should the U.S. and Israel attack again. At the same time, ",["a statement attributed to him","https://www.usnews.com/news/world/articles/2026-11-04/irans-khamenei-says-us-hostility-will-persist-regardless-of-party-in-power"]," indicates that hostilities between the United States and Iran will persist regardless of the balance of party political power in Washington."]},{"k":"p","s":["This raises questions about ",["the prospects for diplomacy","https://www.cnbc.com/2026/10/31/qatar-iran-us-talks-mediation.html"],". During the summer, the U.S. and Iran agreed to an ",["initial 14-point memorandum of understanding","https://arabcenterdc.org/resource/memorandum-of-understanding-between-the-united-states-of-america-and-the-islamic-republic-of-iran/"]," that, if finalized, could have brought a permanent end to the hostilities. But since the ",["60-day clock on that agreement lapsed","https://arabcenterdc.org/resource/memorandum-of-understanding-between-the-united-states-of-america-and-the-islamic-republic-of-iran/"],", no parallel diplomatic agreement has emerged."]},{"k":"h","s":["No practical solution"]},{"k":"p","s":["Even with the major shift in the U.S. political landscape, it remains unclear whether Trump will resume operations against Iran before the new Congress is sworn in. The messy election result in Israel – which has left the ",["pro-war, and potentially outgoing, Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyanu","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/26/netanyahu-reportedly-pressured-israel-military-attack-iran-runup-to-election"]," with potentially more reason to double-down in Iran – only complicates matters."]},{"k":"p","s":["The U.S. military certainly appears to be ready to engage in a new round of attacks against Iran if so directed, and Iran is ready to retaliate. But given ",["the shortcomings in the U.S. inventory","https://nypost.com/2026/09/15/us-news/iran-war-effort-hampered-by-munitions-shortfalls-production-bottlenecks-pentagon-watchdog-finds/"]," – with munitions and missile and air defense capabilities depleted by eight months of war – escalation is something Trump and his inner circle will have to consider with caution."]},{"k":"p","s":["Iran might force the issue by engaging in ",["asymmetric attacks","https://www.cbsnews.com/news/uk-raf-fairford-terror-plot-iran-2-men-charged-security-offenses/"]," in the region or beyond that they have not attempted already. Or it could launch a coordinated offensive with its partners in the region – notably the Houthis in Yemen, who have become more active ",["in their own conflict with Saudi Arabia","https://time.com/article/2026/10/15/who-are-the-houthi-rebels-saudi-arabia-oil-airport-attacks/"]," in recent months."]},{"k":"p","s":["But save an event that the Trump administration perceives is giving it cover to act, there are no clear indications emerging from Washington as to which way it will move."]},{"k":"p","s":["Vance diagnosed a widely perceived political problem for Republicans: Voters don’t want more war. But what he noticeably didn’t mention was a practical solution. The Middle East conflict – and the United States’ role in it – are, as such, locked in a stalemate."]},{"k":"p","s":["America and Iran have both borne significant political, military and economic costs. A decision not to pursue an endgame would leave those sunk; doing so may only increase them."]}],"chars":6957},"https://theconversation.com/pre-election-polls-understated-right-in-nz-with-overhang-skewing-preliminary-results-295738":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"e8d59e6537759e04a28794931429e2405c13836180a18ee916e024254fe975cf","read":"https://theconversation.com/pre-election-polls-understated-right-in-nz-with-overhang-skewing-preliminary-results-295738","bytes":178662,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Pre-election polls understated right in NZ, with overhang skewing preliminary results","by":[{"n":"Adrian Beaumont","r":"Election Analyst (Psephologist) at The Conversation; and Honorary Associate, School of Mathematics and Statistics, The University of Melbourne"}],"pub":"2026-11-08T02:55:32Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Preliminary results from Saturday’s New Zealand election indicate there are a total of 11 ",["overhang seats","https://electionresults.govt.nz/ge2026/index.html"],", with parliament expanded from its nominal 120 seats to 131."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Overhangs occur","https://www.rnz.co.nz/news/politics_election-2026/2408208/explainer-what-is-an-overhang-and-how-could-it-change-the-election-tonight"]," as a result of electors having two votes – one for their local MP and one for their preferred party (which determines overall seat entitlements)."]},{"k":"p","s":["When a party wins more electorate seats than it would be entitled to based on its proportional party vote, more seats have to be added to parliament. An overhang was predicted before the election, but its size has surprised most observers."]},{"k":"p","s":["This will be the largest overhang in a New Zealand election since the mixed member proportional system (MMP) was first ",["first used is 1996","https://elections.nz/democracy-in-nz/what-is-new-zealands-system-of-government/what-is-mmp/the-introduction-of-mmp"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["National’s party vote of 29.2% was just behind Labour’s on 29.4%, which would normally entitle National to 35 seats."]},{"k":"p","s":["But of the 71 electorate seats that are elected by first-past-the-post ballot, National is leading in 42, Labour in 21, Te Pāti Māori in five, the Greens in two and ACT in one."]},{"k":"p","s":["Te Pāti Māori was entitled to one seat on its party vote of 0.6%, but is leading in five of the seven electorates for those on the Māori roll."]},{"k":"p","s":["On the preliminary results, there’s a seven-seat overhang for National and a four-seat overhang for Te Pāti Māori."]},{"k":"p","s":["On current counting, right-wing parties have 67 seats, one more than the 66 needed for a majority. Left-wing parties have 57 seats, and the centrist Opportunity Party has seven."]},{"k":"h","s":["Poll performance"]},{"k":"p","s":["On the preliminary results, right-wing parties (National, ACT and NZ First) were 6.7 points ahead of left-wing parties (Labour, the Greens and Te Pāti Māori) on party list vote shares. This preliminary result has been marked on my poll graph below."]},{"k":"p","s":["On current counting, the right has over-performed all the ",["pre-election polls","https://theconversation.com/nz-election-eve-poll-watch-rights-lead-slipping-with-opportunity-still-the-wild-card-295736"],", with the Curia poll for the Taxpayers’ Union the most accurate."]},{"k":"p","s":["I expect the right’s lead to drop after publication of final results, but the Reid Research poll – the only pollster that had the left leading since July – will be the least accurate of this election."]},{"k":"p","s":["Opportunity – which could potentially hold the balance of power between left and right when final results are in – won 6.0% of the party list vote on the preliminary results."]},{"k":"p","s":["That was well clear of the 5% threshold needed to enter parliament without winning an electorate. ",["Polls had given","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opinion_polling_for_the_2026_New_Zealand_general_election#Table_of_polls"]," Opportunity between 5.1% and 7.2%."]},{"k":"p","s":["If there were no overhangs for either National or Te Pāti Māori, the right would still have won a majority on the preliminary results, as its 6.7-point lead over the left exceeded Opportunity’s 6.0%."]},{"k":"h","s":["Special votes could swing final results"]},{"k":"p","s":["At the ",["2023 election","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2023_New_Zealand_general_election#Results"],", National won the party vote by 38.1% to 26.9% over Labour, an 11.2-point margin. This gave National 44 of the then 72 electorates at that election."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite trailing Labour by 0.2 points so far, National has only lost two electorates at this election."]},{"k":"p","s":["I expect an aggregate of the electorate votes would be better for both National and Te Pāti Māori than their party list votes."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is not the final count. No further updates will be released until final ",["results are published on November 27","https://vote.nz/2026-general-election/about/overview/key-dates"],". In the past, left-wing parties have gained one or two seats from right-wing parties from the preliminary to the final results."]},{"k":"p","s":["National leads Labour in two ",["electorates","https://electionresults.govt.nz/ge2026/electorate-status.html"]," by fewer than 500 votes, in Hamilton East by 456 votes and in Wairarapa by 139 votes."]},{"k":"p","s":["If National eventually loses both seats, the right would have a bare majority with 65 of 129 seats. Shifts to the left on the party vote could put the right below a majority."]},{"k":"p","s":["Te Tai Tokerau is another electorate that could flip on later counting. Te Pāti Māori is leading the Greens by 436 votes. The Greens wouldn’t gain any overall seats if they won this electorate, as it would simply replace a party list seat."]},{"k":"p","s":["That means it would be better for the left-wing parties overall for Te Pāti Māori to win in Te Tai Tokerau."]}],"chars":3877},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/pakistan":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"06114032445f1688512547741b51d54b3ff01a0ccb59f7868a8aefdce1e0b68d","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/pakistan","bytes":117330,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Pakistan travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-21T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-10-27T16:05:20+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pakistan-Afghanistan border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to within 10 miles of the border between Pakistan and Afghanistan."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to these areas in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Province:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Bajaur"]},{"k":"li","s":["Bannu"]},{"k":"li","s":["Buner"]},{"k":"li","s":["Chārsadda"]},{"k":"li","s":["Dera Ismail Khan"]},{"k":"li","s":["Hangu"]},{"k":"li","s":["Karak"]},{"k":"li","s":["Khyber"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kohat"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kurram"]},{"k":"li","s":["Lakki Marwat"]},{"k":"li","s":["Upper Dir"]},{"k":"li","s":["Lower Dir"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mohmand"]},{"k":"li","s":["Orakzai"]},{"k":"li","s":["Peshawar, including the city of Peshawar"]},{"k":"li","s":["Swat"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tank"]},{"k":"li","s":["North Waziristan"]},{"k":"li","s":["Upper South Waziristan"]},{"k":"li","s":["Lower South Waziristan"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Karakoram Highway between Mansehra and Chilas via Battagram, Besham City, Dasu and Sazin up to the junction with the N15"]},{"k":"li","s":["the N45 Highway, from the north of the Mardan ring road, to the edge of Chitral City, including Kalash valley"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to these areas in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Province:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Malakand"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mardan"]},{"k":"li","s":["Nowshera"]},{"k":"li","s":["Shangla"]},{"k":"li","s":["Swabi"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Balochistan Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Balochistan Province."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pakistan-India Border Area"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel within 5 miles of the international border between Pakistan and India. Exceptions are the Grand Trunk highway via the Wagah border (the crossing point is currently closed, however visitors can still access and attend the daily Wagah border ceremony) and the Kartarpur Corridor for Sikh pilgrims visiting Gurdwara Darbar Sahib (currently closed for crossings)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pakistan-administered Kashmir"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to Azad Jammu and Kashmir."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to within 10 miles of the Line of Control."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sindh Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to all areas of Sindh Province north of and including the city of Nawabshah."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Punjab Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to Dera Ghazi Khan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel to these regions","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/pakistan/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency measures in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa"]},{"k":"p","s":["Emergency measures and Governor’s Rule were introduced in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa province on 11 October. There were reports of road closures, possible disruption to public transport, increased security presence, and disruption to internet services in parts of the province."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in or travelling to Khyber Paktunkhwa:"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay away from protests, political gatherings and large crowds"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local news and the advice of local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["check your route before you travel"]},{"k":"li","s":["be prepared to change your travel plans at short notice"]},{"k":"h","s":["Demonstrations in Pakistan-administered Kashmir"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are currently demonstrations in areas of Pakistan-administered Kashmir known locally as “Azad Jammu and Kashmir”."]},{"k":"p","s":["Local authorities have advised visitors to avoid travel to the area, while visitors already there have been encouraged to leave to avoid potential disruption."]},{"k":"p","s":["Demonstrations in the area have led to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["road closures and severe travel disruption"]},{"k":"li","s":["suspension of mobile and internet services"]},{"k":"li","s":["clashes between protestors and security forces, with reports of injuries and loss of life"]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional tensions"]},{"k":"p","s":["The context in the Middle East remains deeply unpredictable and the risk of sudden escalation is high. Since conflict began in early 2026, Iran has stated its intention to target locations associated with the US and Israel, including, but not limited to, organisations, businesses, facilities, and institutions. There have been strikes and retaliatory attacks by Iran and others across the region against civilian and US military infrastructure."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals in, or planning to travel through, the Middle East should be prepared for possible flight cancellations, airspace closures, and travel disruptions. You should:"]},{"k":"p","s":["Global supply routes could affect Pakistan’s fuel availability and pricing. This may lead to transport disruption and delays, in some areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is an ongoing risk of terrorism."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should continue to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["be careful around protests, demonstrations, rallies, security checkpoints, tourist sites, and religious gatherings and sites, particularly in urban areas across Pakistan"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the advice of local authorities and plan ahead to allow extra time for travel and keep up to date with local and international media"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information"]},{"k":"li","s":["be prepared to take shelter, stay indoors, or move to a safe building immediately if the local authorities instruct you to do so"]},{"k":"li","s":["sign up to ",["FCDO Travel Advice email alerts","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/pakistan/email-signup"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read the FCDO’s advice on ",["if you’re affected by a crisis abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["Support during a crisis"]},{"k":"p","s":["If a severe crisis develops in Pakistan, the situation can change quickly including your ability to travel. Regional tensions during May 2025 resulted in sustained airspace closures which caused airlines to suspend flights, domestic travel was also restricted. Practical support from the British government, including face-to-face consular support or evacuation, may be severely limited in a crisis. Read our ",["general guidance on consular support in a crisis.","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Be prepared to re-arrange your own departure from Pakistan at short notice. If it is not safe or possible to leave, you should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay indoors whenever possible, and have a stock of essential supplies such as food, drinking water and medicine"]},{"k":"li","s":["obey any local restrictions such as curfews"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor the media for developments that would allow you to leave safely"]},{"k":"li","s":[["subscribe to our Travel Advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/pakistan/email-signup"]]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the ",["British High Commission social media accounts","https://x.com/ukinpakistan"]," for the latest information"]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/pakistan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Pakistan’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Pakistan set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Pakistan High Commission in London or nearest Pakistani consulate","https://www.phclondon.org/contactus"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Pakistan, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date of your visa application."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped on entry."]},{"k":"p","s":["Leaving Pakistan will be difficult if you do not have an entry stamp. If your passport was not stamped on entry, contact the ",["Ministry of Interior","https://visa.nadra.gov.pk/"]," or visit a National Database and Registration Office (NDRA) office."]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal entry to Pakistan is a serious offence. If you enter without the correct documentation you may be detained or deported. If you enter Pakistan illegally, you may not be able to travel onward from Pakistan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You need a visa to visit Pakistan and you must apply in advance."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["information on visa categories and how to apply","https://visa.nadra.gov.pk/visa-categories/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Visas for journalists often have extra travel restrictions. Follow the terms of your visa, or you could be fined or detained."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also ",["apply for visa extensions","https://visa.nadra.gov.pk/visa-categories/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Returning to the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have an unexpired visa, a Pakistani national identity card or a Pakistani passport to leave Pakistan."]},{"k":"p","s":["If your visa has expired, ",["apply online for an exit permit","https://visa.nadra.gov.pk/exitpermit/"]," from within Pakistan before attempting to travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you do not have evidence of Pakistani nationality and you entered without a visa, contact the ",["Ministry of Interior","https://visa.nadra.gov.pk/"]," or visit a NADRA office."]},{"k":"h","s":["Citizens of Pakistan overseas"]},{"k":"p","s":["The National Identity Card for Overseas Pakistanis (NICOP) or Smart National Identity Card Overseas Pakistanis (SNICOP), are issued to citizens of Pakistan who are not resident in Pakistan. If you hold a valid version of either, you will be recognised as a citizen of Pakistan. You can enter Pakistan without a visa and stay for an unlimited period. See ",["how to apply for Pakistani identity cards","https://www.phclondon.org/nadra"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling with children"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling with a child as a single parent or are not the child’s parent, you may need to provide documentary evidence of parental responsibility before leaving Pakistan. This is particularly likely if the child is of Pakistani origin."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crossing land borders"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) advises against travel to most of the Pakistan-Afghanistan, Pakistan-China and Pakistan-Iran border areas. FCDO advises against all travel to Afghanistan and Iran."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pakistan-Afghanistan border"]},{"k":"p","s":["All borders with Afghanistan can close at short notice. There has been overcrowding and violence at open border crossings."]},{"k":"p","s":["If entering Pakistan via the Torkham border crossing with Afghanistan you will need a valid Pakistan visa."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pakistan-Iran border"]},{"k":"p","s":["All official land border crossings with Iran are located in Balochistan province, where the FCDO advises against all travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Border crossings may be closed at short notice, and access is limited and closely monitored. If entering Pakistan via a land border with Iran, you will need a valid Pakistan visa. Check with local authorities or travel providers for the latest information before attempting to cross."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pakistan-India border"]},{"k":"p","s":["The international border between Pakistan and India is subject to strict controls. The Wagah border crossing on the Grand Trunk Road is the only official land crossing between the two countries, but it is currently closed. However, visitors may still access and attend the daily Wagah border ceremony. The Kartarpur Corridor is currently not in use for Sikh pilgrims visiting Gurdwara Darbar Sahib."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ensure you have the necessary visas and documentation and check with local authorities or travel providers before attempting to cross."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pakistan-China border"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Khunjerab Pass, the only official land border crossing between Pakistan and China, is located on the Karakoram Highway and is open to foreign tourists. It is open seasonally, typically from April to November, but can close at very short notice due to severe weather conditions, particularly snowfall during colder months. Check the weather conditions before you travel as conditions can change at short notice and landslides and snowfall can block the route."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware that border closures may occur without warning on either side, and access to the area is remote and limited. Ensure you have the appropriate Pakistani visa and Chinese entry documentation before attempting to cross. Check with local authorities or your travel provider for the latest updates before travelling to the region."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Pakistan, you must have certificates to prove you’ve had:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"]]},{"k":"li","s":["a polio vaccine, in some circumstances"]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Pakistan guide","https://www.travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/171/pakistan#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health screening"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Mpox"]},{"k":"p","s":["In response to the recent international mpox outbreaks, travellers may experience enhanced screening and preventive measures, including testing, on entry to Pakistan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["more about mpox on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/disease/125/mpox-monkeypox"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods that you can take into and out of Pakistan","https://www.trade.gov/country-commercial-guides/pakistan-customs-regulations"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol and pork"]},{"k":"p","s":["Importing alcohol or pork products is illegal. You could be detained if you try to import them."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/pakistan/warnings-and-insurance"]," and ",["regional risks advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/pakistan/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Pakistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are very likely to try to carry out attacks in Pakistan."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorism and sectarian violence throughout Pakistan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read our advice on ",["regional risks in Pakistan","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/pakistan/regional-risks"]," for information about areas where we advise against travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist groups operating in Pakistan include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tehreek-e Taliban Pakistan (TTP)"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tehreek-e Jihad Pakistan (TJP)"]},{"k":"li","s":["Balochistan separatists"]},{"k":"li","s":["Islamic State Khorasan Province (ISKP)"]},{"k":"li","s":["al-Qa’ida"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist groups mainly target Government of Pakistan security forces. Areas of Balochistan and Khyber Pakhtunkhwa, including Peshawar, and Quetta suffer regular terrorist attacks. Attacks have also taken place in Karachi, Islamabad, Lahore and other major cities. A number of attacks have also taken place against Chinese nationals; some attacks have also targeted individuals of East Asian appearance more generally."]},{"k":"p","s":["While terrorist attacks are mainly directed against the Pakistani state, attacks could be indiscriminate and occur without warning, including in places visited by foreign nationals, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Pakistani government buildings and infrastructure"]},{"k":"li","s":["security, judicial and police force locations"]},{"k":"li","s":["places of worship, including churches and religious sites"]},{"k":"li","s":["hotels, restaurants and shopping areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["schools and educational institutions"]},{"k":"li","s":["popular tourist sites or hiking trails"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be cautious about attending any public event, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["processions, protests, demonstrations and rallies"]},{"k":"li","s":["religious gatherings"]},{"k":"li","s":["sports and live music events"]},{"k":"p","s":["Public transport and transport hubs, including airports, are at risk of attack. Avoid using the railway network due to the risk of terrorist attacks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take particular care during periods of national, social or religious significance, including the month of Ramadan, and during election periods. When travelling, always:"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep a low profile"]},{"k":"li","s":["minimise your exposure to areas and events that pose a higher risk"]},{"k":"li","s":["vary your routes and timings if you make regular journeys"]},{"k":"li","s":["limit movements on Friday afternoons"]},{"k":"li","s":["be prepared to change your plans as necessary"]},{"k":"p","s":["Examples of recent attacks include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["on 6 February 2026, a suicide bombing at the Imam Bargah Mosque in Islamabad killed at least 36 people and injured more than 150; Da’esh (IS) claimed responsibility for the attack"]},{"k":"li","s":["in January 2026, coordinated attacks by the Balochistan Liberation Army (BLA) across multiple towns in Balochistan resulted in the deaths of at least 31 civilians and 17 security personnel. Militants targeted government buildings, security installations, and public areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["on 11 November 2025, a suicide bombing outside Islamabad’s district courts complex killed 12 people and injured more than two dozen"]},{"k":"li","s":["in March 2025, the Jaffar Express passenger train travelling from Quetta to Peshawar, with at least 380 passengers on board, was hijacked by the Balochistan Liberation Army (BLA), resulting in 64 deaths"]},{"k":"li","s":["in October 2024, a suicide attack near Karachi’s Jinnah International Airport killed 4 individuals - including two Chinese nationals and two Pakistani civilians"]},{"k":"li","s":["public service and health officials have been attacked while working on health programmes"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorist kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a threat of kidnap throughout Pakistan, particularly within the Khyber Pakhtunkhwa and Balochistan provinces. Terrorist groups are unlikely to prioritise the kidnap of westerners in Pakistan. Any kidnap of a foreign national by terrorist groups in Pakistan would likely be opportunistic."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals are seen as legitimate targets, including tourists, humanitarian aid workers, journalists and business travellers. If you are kidnapped, the reason for your presence is unlikely to protect you or secure your safe release."]},{"k":"p","s":["The long-standing policy of the British government policy is not to make substantive concessions to hostage takers. The British government considers that paying ransoms and releasing prisoners builds the capability of terrorist groups and finances their activities. This can, in turn, increase the risk of further hostage-taking. The Terrorism Act (2000) makes payments to terrorists illegal."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Political rallies, protests and demonstrations may take place across the country and can start with little warning. Most are peaceful, but they can turn violent quickly and lead to clashes with law enforcement. Individuals near protest activity may face increased scrutiny by security forces. During elections, terrorists have targeted security forces, political events, rallies, government buildings and polling stations."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid all political demonstrations, be mindful of large crowds of people and public events"]},{"k":"li","s":["be mindful of days of political or social significance"]},{"k":"li","s":["be prepared to change your plans as necessary"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep track of the local news"]},{"k":"p","s":["During times of protest or civil unrest, mobile data coverage and internet connectivity may be cut without warning. Additionally, major road networks in and around cities may be shut or blocked. Have alternative travel options such as different routes for any journeys you plan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Street crime is a risk, particularly in crowded areas. Take sensible measures to guard your possessions and reduce your personal risk. Be cautious when moving around urban areas at night, especially when on foot."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is an active black market in forged and stolen passports. Credit card fraud is common. Beware of scams."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Criminal kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals of Pakistani origin have been targeted by criminals, including kidnappers, as they are often perceived as being wealthier than locals."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pakistan is a Muslim country. Respect the local traditions, customs and laws. Make sure your actions do not cause offence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Standards of public behaviour differ between the UK and Pakistan. Behaviour that might be acceptable in the UK can cause offence in Pakistan. Being considerate of others is important in Pakistani culture. Loud or rowdy behaviour in public is likely to attract a negative response."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry photo ID. You may be asked to show it and you might be detained until you can show a valid ID."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan, also called Ramazan in Pakistan, is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. In 2026, Ramadan is expected to start around mid-February and finish around mid-March. During this time, do not:"]},{"k":"li","s":["eat, drink, smoke or chew gum in public in the daytime, including in your car"]},{"k":"li","s":["play loud music or dance"]},{"k":"li","s":["swear in public"]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that if hotels and restaurants are providing food or drink in fasting hours, they may separate you from Islamic guests, for example with screens"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes – clothing that does not meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that fasting can cause tiredness"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that driving may be unpredictable, particularly when people are trying to get home at dusk"]},{"k":"li","s":["be patient and show tolerance"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pakistan is an Islamic country. Dress modestly, men and women should cover their shoulders and legs in public. Women should cover their heads when entering mosques and holy places, and in rural areas."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Blasphemy"]},{"k":"p","s":["Insulting or showing disrespect or contempt of religion, religious beliefs or anything considered holy (blasphemy) is illegal. Blasphemy has a broad definition in Pakistani law. It includes public and private comments in any form, including on social media."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are significant criminal penalties, including the death penalty. Those accused of blasphemy are at significant risk of violence from the public. Both Muslims and religious minorities have been victims of blasphemy accusations and violence, including killings."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be sensitive to religious beliefs and behave appropriately."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Death penalty"]},{"k":"p","s":["The death penalty can be issued for individuals convicted for crimes including, but not limited to, blasphemy, murder and rape."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drinking alcohol is illegal for Muslims. Non-Muslims are allowed to drink in Pakistan, but you must get a licence from the authorities. It is also illegal for non-Muslims to supply alcohol to Muslims. Public drinking and drunkenness are illegal and can lead to detention."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and penalties"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can get a prison sentence for possession of even small quantities of illegal drugs. British nationals have been arrested on drug trafficking charges and have been detained for long periods while their case is in the Pakistan legal system."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking photos in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not take photos at military establishments, airports or any infrastructure (including bridges and dams) or from aircraft. British nationals have been arrested on suspicion of ‘spying’. Check with officials if you’re not sure whether you can take a photo."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should not take photos of people without seeking prior permission."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Property disputes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Disputes over property ownership are common in Pakistan and have been known to become violent. British nationals have been victims of property scams such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["selling the same property to multiple buyers"]},{"k":"li","s":["using forged ownership documents or fake land records"]},{"k":"li","s":["illegal occupation of land or property (‘qabza’), particularly where owners live overseas"]},{"k":"li","s":["selling plots in unapproved or fraudulent housing schemes"]},{"k":"li","s":["impersonating the rightful owner to sell or transfer property"]},{"k":"li","s":["using a Power of Attorney to take control of someone else’s property without their consent"]},{"k":"li","s":["relatives selling inherited or jointly owned property without consent"]},{"k":"li","s":["misuse of rental income or unauthorised management of property"]},{"k":"li","s":["disputes arising from informal or verbal family agreements"]},{"k":"p","s":["The British High Commission cannot get involved in property disputes. Consular staff are not legally trained and cannot provide legal advice or intervene in private legal matters."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are involved in a property dispute, you should seek independent legal advice from an English-speaking lawyer in Pakistan."]},{"k":"p","s":["If your case relates to property in Punjab, you may contact the Overseas Pakistani Cell at the Lahore High Court which deals with legal cases involving Pakistani nationals living overseas."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are concerned for your safety, you should contact the police. The British Government cannot provide private security. If you do wish to have private security, you should consider arranging this for yourself through a private security company."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity between men is illegal. There are occasional arrests, and there are negative attitudes to same-sex relationships throughout Pakistan which can sometimes result in violence. See more details from the Human Dignity Trust about the ",["current application of the law","https://www.humandignitytrust.org/country-profile/pakistan/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Relationships"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal for unmarried couples to live together in Pakistan. The law regarding unmarried people sharing a hotel room does not generally apply to visiting foreign nationals, particularly in popular tourist areas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Planning secure travel around Pakistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must obtain advance permission from local or federal authorities to travel in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa (KP), Balochistan and several districts in Azad Kashmir. There are several prohibited areas across the country, particularly the areas around military installations, nuclear plants, naval and aerial basis. Officials could stop you and ask you to turn back."]},{"k":"p","s":["When travelling in Pakistan be aware of the risks, including carjacking. You or your travel agency should contact the local authorities of your destination in advance to check the local security situation. In areas of higher risk, local authorities sometimes arrange police escorts for your own protection. They will also tell you if you need a No Objection Certificate from the Pakistani Ministry of Interior."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take safety precautions, keep a low profile and choose your accommodation carefully."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Pakistan, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have both the ",["1968 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel. If you don’t have the correct documents to drive, you could be detained and a police report could be registered in your name."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Outside of the major motorways, the quality of roads is variable. Road conditions can be poor. Local driving standards are erratic, especially at night. Take care on long road journeys and when travelling cross-country."]},{"k":"p","s":["The north of Pakistan is mountainous. Many roads, including the N15 highway between Chilas and Babusar in Gilgit Baltistan, are inaccessible at some times of the year due to extreme weather conditions. Many roads in these remote areas are of very poor quality with uneven surfaces. Landslides frequently block or destroy roads. Use experienced local drivers when travelling these routes and only in clear weather conditions."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public transport"]},{"k":"p","s":["Due to the level of crime, avoid using public transport, including the Metro Bus between Rawalpindi and Islamabad."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid using street taxis, e-taxis. or online apps for taxi services. Only use taxis from reputable, licensed companies where you call for a taxi and the operator contacts a taxi driver."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports can be crowded at times and your baggage may need to go through screening equipment and checks. When travelling through an airport, allow enough time to complete check-in and security procedures."]},{"k":"p","s":["Flights to and from the mountainous areas in the north of Pakistan are frequently delayed or cancelled due to extreme weather. Ensure you have alternative routes planned in case of cancellations."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rail travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid using the railway network due to the risk of terrorist attacks and derailments."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The threat from piracy within Pakistan’s territorial waters is low. There is a significant threat of piracy in the Gulf of Aden and other parts of the Indian Ocean. Mariners should follow shipping industry guidelines on precautions to take."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor local and international weather updates from the ",["Pakistan Meteorological Department","https://www.pmd.gov.pk/en/"]," and see weather advisories from the National Disaster Management Authority."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Landslides"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check local forecasts from the Pakistan Meteorological Department and be aware of the risk of landslides and road blockages, particularly in hilly and mountainous regions. Take extreme care crossing swollen rivers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Monsoons and flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pakistan can experience flooding and landslides during monsoon season which is usually from late June to early October. The flooding can affect all provinces in Pakistan. Roads and bridges have been damaged or destroyed, affecting travel in many parts of the country. More information is available from the ",["National Disaster Management Authority","https://cms.ndma.gov.pk/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earth tremors are common. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency has advice on ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Pakistan. It only covers regions where The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/pakistan/warnings-and-insurance"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/pakistan/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to these districts in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Province:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Bajaur"]},{"k":"li","s":["Bannu"]},{"k":"li","s":["Buner"]},{"k":"li","s":["Chārsadda"]},{"k":"li","s":["Dera Ismail Khan"]},{"k":"li","s":["Hangu"]},{"k":"li","s":["Karak"]},{"k":"li","s":["Khyber"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kohat"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kurram"]},{"k":"li","s":["Lakki Marwat"]},{"k":"li","s":["Upper Dir"]},{"k":"li","s":["Lower Dir"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mohmand"]},{"k":"li","s":["Orakzai"]},{"k":"li","s":["Peshawar, including the city of Peshawar"]},{"k":"li","s":["Swat"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tank"]},{"k":"li","s":["North Waziristan"]},{"k":"li","s":["Upper South Waziristan"]},{"k":"li","s":["Lower South Waziristan"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to these areas in Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Province:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Malakand"]},{"k":"li","s":["Mardan"]},{"k":"li","s":["Nowshera"]},{"k":"li","s":["Shangla"]},{"k":"li","s":["Swabi"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against travel to much of Khyber Pakhtunkhwa Province. There is frequent militant violence in the former Federally Administered Tribal Areas. Local authorities may impose curfews at short notice and there is frequent military activity. Cross-border attacks may occur in the surrounding areas south and west of Chitral."]},{"k":"h","s":["N45 Highway between Mardan and Chitral"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel on the N45 Highway, from the north of the Mardan ring road, to the edge of the city of Chitral because of high crime and terrorism incidents."]},{"k":"h","s":["Balochistan Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Balochistan Province."]},{"k":"p","s":["The situation at the Pakistan-Iran border can be unpredictable. In January 2024 both Iran and Pakistan conducted missile and drone strikes targeting militant groups on either side of their border."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high risk from kidnapping and militant activity in much of Balochistan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Pakistan-administered Kashmir"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to Azad Jammu and Kashmir."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to within 10 miles of the India-Pakistan border area within Pakistan-administered Kashmir, known as the Line of Control."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there is a ceasefire in place, there are still significant tensions between India and Pakistan. There is a risk of small arms fire and occasional mortar fire."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have the necessary permissions to travel. Check the latest requirements before you travel as they can change."]},{"k":"h","s":["Sindh Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to all areas of Sindh Province north of and including the city of Nawabshah."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are high levels of lawlessness in the north of Sindh Province. There is a very high risk of crime and kidnapping. Criminal gangs and bandits with access to heavy weaponry are active in the area. In 2022, a large criminal gang attacked police in Ghotki, northern Sindh, killing several officers and taking other officers hostage."]},{"k":"h","s":["Gilgit-Baltistan region"]},{"k":"p","s":["Gilgit‑Baltistan Assembly elections are scheduled for 7 June 2026. Political activity around election periods in Pakistan can lead to disruption, heightened security presence, and restrictions on movement. Roads, including major routes, may be blocked or closed without warning, and travel times may be significantly longer than usual. Monitor local media for updates and continue to follow FCDO travel advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Flight schedules to Gilgit and Skardu Airports in the north of Pakistan may be unreliable and may change at short notice. Check with your airline or travel agent."]},{"k":"p","s":["Road routes are also likely to be restricted by seasonal weather, with the Babusar Pass liable to close due to snowfall."]},{"k":"p","s":["The terrain in Gilgit-Baltistan is mountainous, with remote and isolated locations that are difficult to police. You are strongly advised to get local security advice and make appropriate personal security arrangements before you visit."]},{"k":"p","s":["All foreign nationals must register with the local authorities when visiting Gilgit-Baltistan. You might need a permit for mountaineering or trekking, particularly for mountains over 6,000 metres. The permission process can take up to 2 months and is best organised through a travel company. The validity of your travel insurance policy may be affected if you do not have the correct permits."]},{"k":"p","s":["Use reputable trekking agencies, stay on established routes, and always walk in groups. Do not trek alone. If you’re travelling near the border with China read the information on ‘Border areas’ on this page."]},{"k":"h","s":["Karakoram Highway (Khyber Pakhtunkhwa and Gilgit-Baltistan)"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Karakoram Highway runs from Hasan Abdal in north Punjab towards Gilgit and the Chinese border. FCDO advises against all travel on the Highway between Mansehra and Chilas via Battagram, Besham City, Dasu and Sazin up to the junction with the N15."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid travelling on the Highway at night, as the road can be narrow with steep drops. All sections of the Highway north of Battagram up to the Chinese border have experienced landslides."]},{"k":"h","s":["Islamabad"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police and security agencies have a significant presence in Islamabad. Exercise caution in the outlying districts, such as I-8, I-9, I-10, and I-11 and areas further west, where security forces have led operations against suspected criminals and terrorists."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid all protests. Crowded areas such as the Red Mosque (Lal Masjid), Aabpara Market in G-6, and the Islamabad Press Club have been a focal point for protests."]},{"k":"h","s":["Karachi"]},{"k":"p","s":["Levels of violence can vary but there has been a recent increase in armed robbery. The safety of daily activity can be unpredictable. Criminal and political violence is common, including armed carjacking, robbery, kidnap and murder. Strikes called by religious and political parties can cause significant disruption and sometimes lead to violent civil unrest. Smaller-scale labour strikes are also common and cause regular disruptions locally."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of violence in parts of the city which include government offices. Major hotels and the financial district are generally seen as more stable, though there remains a risk of violence, particularly after Friday prayers. See the ",["Terrorism section","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/pakistan/safety-and-security#terrorism"]," for more information on terror threats."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["plan any travel in the city carefully"]},{"k":"li","s":["take advice from hosts or trusted contacts, follow instructions from law enforcement officers and be prepared to cancel or cut back your plans"]},{"k":"li","s":["be especially vigilant in Lyari, Malir, Quaidabad, Orangi Town, Baldia Town, New Karachi Town, Surjani Town and Gulistan-e-Jouhar – they have a greater risk of violence based on past activity"]},{"k":"h","s":["Lahore"]},{"k":"p","s":["Lahore is the capital of Punjab and attracts large numbers of tourists and business travellers. While the city has a widespread police presence, there have been recent terrorist attacks. These have targeted public places and government or security forces. Avoid religious events or gatherings, public events and large crowds of people."]},{"k":"h","s":["Punjab"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to Dera Ghazi Khan."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you travel to southern Punjab take advice about the local security situation in advance. There is a high level of crime and public order incidents."]},{"k":"h","s":["Border areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) advises against all but essential travel to within:"]},{"k":"p","s":["5 miles of the border with India, with the exception of official land crossings (see ",["‘Crossing land borders’ section","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/pakistan/entry-requirements#crossing-land-borders"],")"]},{"k":"p","s":["Except for official border crossing points, foreign nationals are not allowed to travel within certain distances of Pakistan’s international borders. This includes travel to within:"]},{"k":"li","s":["10 miles of the Line of Control"]},{"k":"li","s":["10 miles of the border with China, with the exception of official land crossings (see ",["‘Crossing land borders’ section","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/pakistan/entry-requirements#crossing-land-borders"],")"]},{"k":"li","s":["10 miles of the border with Afghanistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you travel to these areas you may face risks of kidnapping, high levels of militancy and other crime."]},{"k":"p","s":["The situation for border crossings between Afghanistan and Pakistan may change rapidly due to the security situation in Afghanistan. See ",["Afghanistan travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/afghanistan"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 1122 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Response time varies, particularly between urban and rural areas. In remote or mountainous regions it could take over an hour due to poor road access and limited ambulance availability."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest vaccinations and health risks in ",["TravelHealthPro’s Pakistan guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/171/pakistan#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Polio vaccination programme"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pakistan is rolling out a widespread polio vaccination programme in an effort to eradicate polio. You should provide proof of polio vaccination if asked by a vaccination team. Any exemption due to a medical condition needs to be supported by a medical certificate issued by recognised health authority."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Altitude sickness"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Pakistan, including Gilgit-Baltistan. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bottled water"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when buying bottled water and follow advice on ",["TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/44/food-and-water-hygiene"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air Pollution"]},{"k":"p","s":["Air pollution is a health hazard in Pakistan, especially during the winter months from October to February. Punjab is one of the worst affected regions, particularly Lahore."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about the ",["risks of poor outdoor air quality on TravelHealthPro","https://www.travelhealthpro.org.uk/disease/219/outdoor-air-quality"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are often shortages of medicine in Pakistan. Some imported goods, including medical supplies, may also be restricted. Make sure to plan for this and keep a good supply of any medicine and medical supplies you need. If you run out of medicine, get advice from a local pharmacy. Some pharmacies, particularly in cities and hospitals, are open 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. If your usual medicine is not available or you need a prescription:"]},{"k":"li","s":["visit a local doctor"]},{"k":"li","s":["speak to your UK doctor for advice on alternative medicines that may be available"]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Pakistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Pakistan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/pakistan-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["The standard of local medical facilities is lower than in the UK, especially in remote areas. Private medical care is expensive but available in all major cities. Specialised treatment for psychiatric illnesses may not be available outside major cities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Pakistan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 1122 (ambulance, fire)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 15"]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you or your parents were born in Pakistan, you might be considered a Pakistani national by the local authorities even if you do not hold a Pakistani passport."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are a dual British-Pakistani national living or travelling in Pakistan, the FCDO will not normally support you or get involved in dealings between you and the Pakistani authorities. Read more about ",["who the FCDO can support abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/who-the-fcdo-can-support-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Pakistan"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Pakistan"],", and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Pakistan"]," in Pakistan"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Pakistan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/information-for-bereaved-families-and-friends-in-pakistan"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Pakistan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/pakistan-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/pakistan/british-high-commission-islamabad"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/pakistan/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Pakistan","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-pakistan"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":40678,"change":"Updated information about regional tensions (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)"},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tonga":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"d1fd274c8127e059acceadb2dfc8c990e751436c2f0a8111a7f4d2d3cb3dfa02","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/tonga","bytes":58191,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Tonga travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-30T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-03-19T14:02:58+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tonga/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Tonga’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Tonga set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the Tongan High Commission in London."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7724 5828"]},{"k":"p","s":["Email: office@tongahighcom.co.uk"]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Tonga, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Tonga without a pre-arranged visa for up to 30 days. Border officials will issue a free visa on when you arrive. You may need to show:"]},{"k":"li","s":["an onward or return ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["sufficient funds – a bank statement is acceptable evidence"]},{"k":"li","s":["confirmed accommodation such as a hotel booking or letter of invitation"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Extending your visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["To extend your stay, contact the ",["Tonga Immigration Department","https://www.revenue.gov.to/immigration-and-general-services"],". Make sure you do not overstay your visa."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Tonga guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/224/tonga#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Tonga","https://www.revenue.gov.to/immigration-and-general-services"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty, including all plant, animal and food products."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must also declare any personal valuables worth 500 Tongan pa’angas (about £160) or more."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Tonga"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques on the customs declaration form if the value is more than 10,000 pa’angas. You may need to pay duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Tonga"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Tonga, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["The level of serious crime is low, but petty theft is fairly common. To protect yourself and your property:"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not leave bags unattended"]},{"k":"li","s":["use hotel safes or deposit boxes for passports and valuables"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay in well-lit and populated areas after dark"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep villas and hotel rooms locked and secure"]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Customs and dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tongan society is very conservative and highly religious. People strictly observe the Sabbath. On Sundays, local people may consider recreational activities to be disrespectful. This does not apply to island resorts."]},{"k":"p","s":["Topless sunbathing and nudity in public is illegal. You could be fined up to 100 pa’angas or get a prison sentence of up to 4 months if you refuse to pay."]},{"k":"p","s":["Swimwear is acceptable on the beach or by streams and waterfalls, but in other areas it is likely to receive negative attention."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Mobile phone coverage"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can buy a local SIM card at the airport. You register it by giving your personal ID. Network coverage is usually reliable in towns, but can be patchy in rural locations."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to drink alcohol in public except at bars or restaurants. The legal drinking age is 21. It is illegal for anyone aged 20 or under to buy alcohol. Drunken behaviour is likely to receive negative attention from locals."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drug taking in all forms is illegal. The maximum penalty for importing or exporting illegal drugs is 30 years’ hard labour and fines of several hundred thousand US dollars. If you are found guilty of cultivating or distributing illegal drugs, you are likely to receive a severe punishment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity between men is illegal in Tonga and the law is occasionally enforced. Same-sex partners showing affection in public may receive negative attention."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming and surfing safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take local advice before swimming or surfing. Tonga’s tides can produce powerful currents in ocean lagoons. There have been fatal accidents on popular beaches."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many waves break directly on to reefs. The sea and beaches may have loose rocks and other debris resulting from the underwater eruption of the Hunga Tonga-Hunga Ha’apai volcano. Take extra care when swimming."]},{"k":"p","s":["For more advice, see ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scuba diving"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before scuba diving, check you are covered by your insurance. You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["ask for the dive operator’s credentials"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure safety equipment and oxygen is available on the boat"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for damage before using any equipment"]},{"k":"li","s":["insist on training and ask operators to explain safe practices"]},{"k":"li","s":["check what to do if something goes wrong, including how to call for help while at sea"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is currently no hyperbaric chamber on Tonga, so get advice from your dive instructor or dive team."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Whale boats"]},{"k":"p","s":["Thousands of whales frequent the waters of Tonga every year between June and November. There are strict regulations on whale watching. It is illegal to swim or kayak with whales unless you are on a licensed boat with a certified guide. If convicted, you could get a fine of up to 5,000 pa’angas or an 18-month prison sentence – or both. The authorities can apply these penalties to a first-time offence."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Tonga, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],". You can drive using your UK driving licence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Roads are generally in good condition, but inland they can be narrow and potholed. Speed limits are low and traffic police can issue on-the-spot fines if you exceed them. All drivers and front seat passengers must wear seatbelts. It is illegal to use a mobile phone while driving."]},{"k":"p","s":["When driving near villages watch for children and animals on the roads. Avoid driving at night as roads are poorly lit and hazards such as livestock and pedestrians make driving very dangerous."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Safety at sea, particularly on board older vessels, is a concern in Tonga. Ferries do not follow normal safety regulations and are often overloaded. Consider carrying your own lifejacket."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Severe weather can cause flight delays and cancellations. Stay in touch with your travel provider."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tropical cyclones"]},{"k":"p","s":["The tropical cyclone season normally runs from November to May, but cyclones can happen throughout the year. During the cyclone season there is a greater risk of severe weather including strong winds and heavy rain. Severe weather may cause floods, landslides, road closures and disrupt essential services and infrastructure. You should follow local advice and monitor local and international weather updates from World Meteorological Organization or ",["Tonga Meteorological Services","https://met.gov.to/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes and tsunamis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tonga is part of the Pacific Ring of Fire, a zone of frequent earthquakes and volcanic eruptions. Earthquakes and volcanic activity can happen at any time and trigger tsunamis. Check advice from local Tongan authorities and ",["tsunami alerts for the region","https://tsunami.gov/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"]," or ",["tsunami","https://www.ready.gov/tsunamis"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 933 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Tonga","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/224/tonga#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Tonga","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/224/tonga"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue (Tongatapu, Vava’u and ‘Eua)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Tonga"]},{"k":"p","s":["Health facilities in Tonga are basic. The range of drugs available is limited and modern equipment is in short supply. Medical evacuation from Tonga is required for most non-basic medical problems."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Emergency services in Tonga"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 911 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 999"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 922"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 933"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/tonga/british-high-commission-nuku"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/tonga/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":12326,"change":"Updated information about global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/thanksgiving-dinner-is-likely-to-be-served-with-a-side-of-political-disagreement-296642":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-18T02:46Z","sha":"8f8bdd6b9470af7bc6635af9b3c589a9663e9b4e85372dee79aaa763c5798a55","read":"https://theconversation.com/thanksgiving-dinner-is-likely-to-be-served-with-a-side-of-political-disagreement-296642","bytes":179447,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Thanksgiving dinner is likely to be served with a side of political disagreement","by":[{"n":"Matthew W. Kreuter","r":"Kahn Family Professor of Public Health, Washington University in St. Louis"},{"n":"Kimberly Johnson","r":"Professor of Public Health, Washington University in St. Louis"},{"n":"Rachel Garg","r":"Assistant Professor of Public Health, Washington University in St. Louis"}],"pub":"2026-11-18T01:38:09Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Every year as Thanksgiving approaches, news stories are written about how holiday gatherings bring together people who see the world very differently, sometimes ",["leading to uncomfortable dinner conversations","https://www.news-press.com/story/opinion/2026/11/07/navigating-uncomfortable-thanksgiving-conversations-opinion/92618504007/"],". ",["The stories usually include advice","https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/health-wellness/how-to-handle-your-stressful-family-at-thanksgiving/92223489007/"]," about avoiding awkward moments and topics that are off-limits, and navigating heated conversations if they arise."]},{"k":"p","s":["As ",["experts in health communication","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1111/1468-0009.12040"]," and public health, we are keenly aware of how conversations with family members and close friends ",["shape people’s decisions and actions","https://doi.org/10.1080/10410236.2022.2114768"]," and that sometimes the ",["benefits of having difficult conversations","https://doi.org/10.1080/00909882.2013.781659"]," outweigh the potential costs. We wondered how often difficult conversations actually take place at Thanksgiving meals and what the conversations are about."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although studies have demonstrated that Thanksgiving meals involving people with diverse political viewpoints were ",["shorter by 24 minutes","https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0239988"]," than meals among people holding similar views, we found no estimates of how often these conversations occur."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our survey of 354 adults from 17 states found that over half – 57% – will share a Thanksgiving meal this year with at least one person from outside their household who sees the world very differently than they do. In 4 out of 5 of these cases, the way their viewpoints differ is politics."]},{"k":"p","s":["The survey participants were initially recruited to represent differing perspectives on health; they were not randomly selected to represent the general population. That means the survey’s findings may not be generalizable beyond the study sample."]},{"k":"h","s":["Table talk: What do Americans expect this Thanksgiving?"]},{"k":"p","s":["From Nov. 7-9, 2026, we surveyed 354 adults from 17 states about their plans for this year’s Thanksgiving. Respondents were part of an ongoing ",["health knowledge monitoring and response system","https://hcrl.wustl.edu/iheard-usa/"],". Their mean age was 47.1 years; three-quarters of them were women; and they were racially and ethnically diverse, with 44% white, 33% African American, 15% Hispanic ethnicity and 8% another race or ethnicity. About 1 in 10 were rural residents, and 43% had children under 18 living in their home."]},{"k":"p","s":["The questions about Thanksgiving meals were sent to 430 people on Nov. 7; 354 completed a survey, which is an 82% response rate."]},{"k":"p","s":["Of the 354 respondents, 80% expected to share a meal with family members or friends from outside their household during the upcoming Thanksgiving holiday."]},{"k":"p","s":["Those planning to share a meal with others from outside their household were then asked, “Holiday meals sometimes bring together people from different generations, with different views, or different life experiences. Thinking about your upcoming Thanksgiving meal, will anyone be there who sees the world very differently than you do?”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Almost 71% of those planning to share a meal with others outside their household said yes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Asked “What are those differences about?” by far the most common response was politics, at 81%, followed by religion at almost 58%, differing views about people such as their career choices or relationships at 54%, health at 53%; and half of the respondents said money. A few mentioned other differences such as “raising children” and “parenting” and “gender expression” and “LGBTQ.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Asked if they think any of those differences will be expressed during the meal, almost 60% said yes. This was especially true for differences in politics. A large majority – 79% – of respondents said that differences in politics would be expressed during the meal. Fewer respondents – 40% or less – expected that differences in views about people, money, religion or health would be expressed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Then our questions got to who is expected to disagree – and what respondents anticipate the disagreements will be about. These responses varied by race and ethnicity."]},{"k":"p","s":["White respondents were more likely than African American or Hispanic respondents to say that others at their Thanksgiving meal will view politics differently from them. African American respondents were more likely than White or Hispanic respondents to say that others at their meal will view money matters differently and were more likely than Hispanics to say that others at their meal will view certain people differently."]},{"k":"p","s":["In short, it’s highly common for those gathered around any Thanksgiving table this year to have different views on key matters, but the differences you’re most likely to hear about during mealtime conversation are political."]},{"k":"h","s":["The value in disagreeing"]},{"k":"p","s":["Science tells us that ",["conflict resolution improves through dialogue","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jesp.2012.02.017"]," by ",["reducing stereotypes and changing attitudes","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.copsyc.2023.101696"]," that tend to divide people. Holiday meals could provide some clues about how Americans navigate conversations with those who hold different viewpoints from them on politics, religion, money and health."]},{"k":"p","s":["As one panel member commented: “I don’t keep people around just because they agree with me on something. I don’t cut people away because we disagree about something.”"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Tori De La Vega","https://hcrl.wustl.edu/people/victoria-de-la-vega/"]," contributed to this story."]}],"chars":4915}};
